      // Notes
      lsoNote1Title: 'Summer Goals!! \u{1F31E}',
      lsoNote1Content: '\u2022 Learn to cook 3 new recipes\n\u2022 Go hiking at least twice a month\n\u2022 Read 2 books\n\u2022 Be a better friend\n\u2022 Start that project I keep talking about\n\u2022 Say yes to things more often\n\nThis is going to be the best summer.',
      lsoNote2Title: 'Things I\'m grateful for',
      lsoNote2Content: '\u2022 Jordan \u2014 always knows how to make me laugh\n\u2022 Mom\'s cooking (and patience)\n\u2022 The squad\n\u2022 That new friend Taylor \u2014 feels like a good one\n\u2022 Summer evenings\n\u2022 The fact that I can start over any time I want',
      lsoNote3Title: 'Good day',
      lsoNote3Content: 'Went to the beach with everyone today. Sam fell asleep and got the worst tan lines. Jordan made us all do a ranking of the clouds.\n\nI laughed so hard my stomach hurt.\n\nI want to remember this feeling.',
      lsoNote4Title: 'Summer Goals (updated)',
      lsoNote4Content: '<span class="crossed">\u2022 Learn to cook 3 new recipes</span>\n<span class="crossed">\u2022 Go hiking at least twice a month</span>\n\u2022 Read 2 books\n<span class="crossed">\u2022 Be a better friend</span>\n<span class="crossed">\u2022 Start that project I keep talking about</span>\n<span class="crossed">\u2022 Say yes to things more often</span>\n\n...maybe next month',
      lsoNote5Title: 'Unsent message to Jordan',
      lsoNote5Content: '<div class="unsent">I don\'t know how to explain it. It\'s not that I don\'t care. I care so much it hurts. I just can\'t seem to\n\nI don\'t know why I can\'t just\n\nYou deserve better than</div>\n\n[draft deleted]',
      lsoNote6Title: 'Why',
      lsoNote6Content: 'Why is it so hard to do the simplest things\n\nI used to be someone who showed up\n\nNow I can\'t even reply to a text\n\nI opened Jordan\'s message today. Read the whole thing. My thumb hovered over the keyboard for ten minutes.\n\nNothing came out.',
      lsoNote7Title: 'The people I\'m letting down',
      lsoNote7Content: 'Jordan\nMom\nMika\nSam\nTaylor\nGrandma\n\n...me',
      lsoNote8Title: '',
      lsoNote8Content: 'tired',
      lsoNote9Title: 'If anyone finds this phone\u2014',
      lsoNote9Content: 'If anyone finds this phone\u2014\n\nI want you to know that the people in these messages are the best people I\'ve ever known. They tried. They really tried.\n\nI just couldn\'t\n\n<span class="incomplete">|</span>',
      // Choices
      lsoCh1Prompt: 'Alex stares at the message. What runs through their mind?',
      lsoCh1Opt1Label: '"No. You\'re the only thing that\'s right."',
      lsoCh1Opt1Thought: 'Alex\'s eyes sting. They type "no" and delete it three times.',
      lsoCh1Opt2Label: '"I wish it were that simple."',
      lsoCh1Opt2Thought: 'Alex sets the phone face-down on the table and stares at the ceiling for a long time.',
      lsoCh1Opt3Label: '...',
      lsoCh1Opt3Thought: 'Alex reads the message. Reads it again. Locks the phone.',
      lsoCh2Prompt: 'Jordan\'s words hang in the air. Alex...',
      lsoCh2Opt1Label: 'Starts typing. Stops. Types again. Deletes everything.',
      lsoCh2Opt1Thought: '"I want to let you in. I just forgot where I put the door."',
      lsoCh2Opt2Label: 'Just stares at the screen until it goes dark.',
      lsoCh2Opt2Thought: 'The screen times out. Alex doesn\'t turn it back on.',
      lsoCh3Prompt: 'Mom wants Alex to come home.',
      lsoCh3Opt1Label: '"Yes!! I\'ll be there \u{1F60A}" (Alex never goes)',
      lsoCh3Opt1Thought: 'Alex types the message with full intention of going. Sunday comes and goes.',
      lsoCh3Opt2Label: '"Maybe, I\'ll let you know"',
      lsoCh3Opt2Thought: 'Alex means it as a yes. But "maybe" becomes their most honest word.',
      lsoCh3Opt3Label: 'Leave it on read',
      lsoCh3Opt3Thought: 'Alex sees the message. The thought of the house, the smells, the warmth \u2014 it\'s too much.',
      lsoCh4Prompt: 'The squad wants Alex there. Alex wants to be there too. But...',
      lsoCh4Opt1Label: '"YESSS count me in!! \u{1F389}" (Alex cancels day-of)',
      lsoCh4Opt1Thought: 'Saturday morning. Alex is dressed. Standing by the door. They text "sorry something came up" and go back to bed.',
      lsoCh4Opt2Label: '"honestly not feeling great, you guys go ahead"',
      lsoCh4Opt2Thought: 'It\'s the most honest thing Alex has said in weeks. No one knows how much it cost to send.',
      lsoCh4Opt3Label: 'Don\'t reply',
      lsoCh4Opt3Thought: 'The notification badge sits there for three days before Alex clears it without reading.',
      lsoCh5Prompt: 'A new friend reaching out. Simple. Easy. But nothing feels simple anymore.',
      lsoCh5Opt1Label: '"Sure! How about Thursday?" (cancels Wednesday night)',
      lsoCh5Opt1Thought: 'Alex genuinely wants to go. That\'s what makes the cancellation text so hard to send.',
      lsoCh5Opt2Label: '"I appreciate it but I\'m not up for it lately"',
      lsoCh5Opt2Thought: 'Taylor\'s kindness makes this harder, not easier.',
      lsoCh5Opt3Label: 'Read. No reply.',
      lsoCh5Opt3Thought: 'Another person to disappoint. The list keeps growing.',
      lsoCh6Prompt: 'The final entry is incomplete. What does the silence mean to you?',
      lsoCh6Opt1Label: 'A pause. Not an ending. Alex will finish this sentence someday.',
      lsoCh6Opt2Label: 'A goodbye they couldn\'t finish writing.',
      lsoCh6Opt3Label: 'That\'s not for us to decide.',

